# No trailing slash on purpose: a worktree may have node_modules as a *symlink* to a
# sibling checkout's copy rather than a real directory, and `node_modules/` matches
# directories only — which left the symlink showing up as an untracked file forever.
node_modules
dist/
.DS_Store
.aider*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv
art-sheet.png
tower-contact-sheet.png

# Accounts and saves live here (tools/accounts.ts); LOOTSIM_DB moves it. Anchored to the
# repo root on purpose — an unanchored `data/` also matches `src/data/`, which silently
# blackholed any *new* file added there (already-tracked files were unaffected, which is
# why this went unnoticed) until this rule was scoped down.
/data/
inworld-sheet.png

# Throwaway measurement scripts. `_scratch-ab.mjs` (a Playwright A/B harness) got swept
# into a commit by a `git add -A` that was meant to pick up three source files — a scratch
# file is exactly what should never be committed, and the naming convention was already
# there to be honoured.
_scratch-*
